## [ISSUE] Guest blacklist and dedupe are case-sensitive and skip base-email normalisation

**Severity:** MEDIUM -- `BLACKLISTED_GUEST_EMAILS` can be bypassed trivially.

### The Problem
```ts
const blacklistedGuestEmails = ...split(",").map((email) => email.toLowerCase())
const uniqueGuests = guests.filter(
  (guest) =>
    !booking.attendees.some((attendee) => guest === attendee.email) &&
    !blacklistedGuestEmails.includes(guest)
);
```
The blacklist is lower-cased but `guest` is not, so `Spam@Example.com` is not matched by `spam@example.com`. `zod.email()` does not lower-case.

### Theory / Proof
The booking-creation path already handles this: `handleNewBooking.ts:741-745` computes `extractBaseEmail(guest).toLowerCase()` and compares against lower-cased blacklist entries, so `foo+tag@x.com` and `FOO@x.com` are blocked. The new endpoint diverges from that established rule. The attendee comparison has the same case issue, so `Alice@x.com` is added as a duplicate of `alice@x.com`.

### Recommendation
```ts
const normalized = (e: string) => extractBaseEmail(e).toLowerCase();
const existing = new Set(booking.attendees.map((a) => a.email.toLowerCase()));
const uniqueGuests = [...new Set(guests.map((g) => g.toLowerCase()))].filter(
  (g) => !existing.has(g) && !blacklistedGuestEmails.some((b) => b === normalized(g))
);
```
